SnapBite — source-available, not open source
============================================

This repository is published so people can read how SnapBite works, verify what
it does with their data, and learn from it. It is not licensed for reuse.

You may:
  - read, study and discuss this code;
  - use the hosted SnapBite bot and Mini App as an end user, under their own
    terms;
  - quote short excerpts with attribution for review, teaching or commentary.

You may not, without written permission from the copyright holder:
  - copy this code into another project, in whole or in substantial part;
  - modify it, or distribute modified or unmodified copies of it;
  - deploy or host it as a service, free or paid;
  - use the SnapBite name, logo or bot handle in a derivative product.

No warranty: this software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
express or implied, including but not limited to the warranties of
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and noninfringement. In no
event shall the author be liable for any claim, damages or other liability
arising from, out of or in connection with the software or its use.

Nutrition values produced by SnapBite are estimates, not medical or dietary
advice. Do not rely on them for a medical condition; consult a qualified
professional.

For permission, collaboration or a different licence: open an issue on
https://github.com/lgf2111/snapbite or contact the author at
https://leeguanfeng.com

---

Switching to a permissive licence (MIT, Apache-2.0) later is a one-line change
to this file; it cannot be done the other way round for releases already
published under a permissive one. That is why the default here is conservative.
